=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web page (web/src/features/sharing/pages/SharingTripsPage.tsx, 222 lines) is the
"Share a trip" surface: it surfaces recent trips eligible for sharing, the static
share-card hint, and the propose-only AI share-card image-prompt drafter. Data
source: `useTrips({ vehicle_id, limit: 20 }) → GET /trips`. SI display contract:
`total_distance_m` is SI metres converted at the render boundary via
`convertDistanceFromSI` + `useUnits`; `total_energy_wh` is rendered verbatim in Wh
(the web row does NOT convert energy). The recent-trips list is the only selector;
clicking a row swaps `selectedTripId`, which the AI card consumes via its `tripId`.

Parity manifest record (13 = 2 panels + 3 states + 8 strings):
  panels  : GlassPanel1 (recent trips), GlassPanel2 (static share-card hint)
  charts  : 0     maps : 0
  states  : loading, empty, success
  strings : 8 sharing.trips.* keys (web key names)

PREDECESSOR / COLLISION FINDING (binding for the whole implementation):
  A sibling Sharing port already exists at apps/apple/Sources/Features/Sharing/
  SharedDrive* (the public `/s/:token` report) with PUBLIC symbols `SharedDrivePage`,
  `SharedDrivePageModel`, `SharedDriveStrings`, …. Both `Sources/` and
  `TeslaSync/Features/` compile into the SINGLE `TeslaSync` module (project.yml), and
  Swift forbids (a) two same-name types and (b) two same-basename files in one target.
  Pre-grep confirmed ZERO existing `SharingTrips`/`SharingTrip` symbols and ZERO
  `SharingTrips*` file basenames. Resolution: every type + file in this unit is
  `SharingTrips…`-prefixed and the shared P2 tokens / P3 components / P1 Units facade
  are REUSED (DRY), not duplicated. The unit lives in the prescribed directory
  apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Sharing/.

STRING-CATALOG FINDING:
  Localizable.xcstrings carried only `translation.sharing.trips.*` (web-import
  namespace), not the bare keys the SwiftUI views resolve (the same convention the
  sibling uses: bare `share.header` exists alongside `translation.share.header`).
  The 8 bare `sharing.trips.*` keys were added with the verbatim web English
  defaults (en), matching the bare-key entry format; JSON re-validated (11844 keys).

AI-SECTION FINDING (third web region, faithful composition, not a counted item):
  The web page's third FadeIn block mounts `<AITripPostcardShareCardImageGeneration
  tripId={selectedTripId} />`. That AI surface is a SEPARATE already-shipped parity
  unit at apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AITripPostcardShareCardImageGeneration*
  (public `AITripPostcardShareCardImageGeneration(tripID: Int?)`). To avoid scope
  narrowing AND avoid stubbing (ADR-011), this page COMPOSES that existing surface
  fed the selected trip id — exactly the web composition. It is not one of the 13
  manifest parity items (it owns its own ledger row), so it is excluded from the
  PARITY count but reproduces the web page's anonymous AI region verbatim.

=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Sharing/   (7 files, 692 lines)
  SharingTripsModels.swift            SharingTrip (SI) + state enum + SharingTripsDataSource seam
  SharingTripsStrings.swift           the 8 web keys (LocalizedStringKey) + count formatters + rawKeys
  SharingTripsFormat.swift            date / duration / distance(SI→display) / energy(Wh) — web parity
  SharingTripsSampleData.swift        Sample (success) + Empty (empty) + Failing (error) data sources
  SharingTripsPageModel.swift         @Observable model: load / refresh / select; state machine
  SharingTripsPage.swift              adaptive scaffold + GlassPanel1/2 + loading/empty/success + row + AI
  SharingTripsRouteRegistration.swift NavigationDestination + /sharing/trips deep-link parser

Design notes:
  - @Observable `SharingTripsPageModel` consumes a KMP-bindable data-source seam
    (`loadTrips` ← useTrips / GET /trips?vehicle_id=&limit=); the view holds no
    networking (ADR-004). `selectedTripID` is the AI card's input (web selectedTripId).
  - SI only on the model; conversion at the SwiftUI render boundary via `Units`
    (P1/S5) + `@Environment(\.tsUnits)` (ADR-005). Distance converts SI metres to the
    user's unit + integer-formats + appends the unit (web fmtInt(convertDistanceFromSI)
    + unit); energy renders verbatim Wh at the user's precision (web fmtNumber, no
    energy-unit conversion) — nothing non-SI is stored or computed.
  - Adaptive macOS + iOS: ScrollView + reflowing rows, 920pt max content width, the
    `.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode` is iOS-gated; one adaptive SwiftUI source (ADR-002/006).
  - a11y: each row is a Button with combined children + the VoiceOver `isSelected`
    trait; the list is a labelled container; dynamic Color.TS (light/dark/contrast),
    Dynamic Type via Font.TS, ≥44pt tap targets.
  - Data source is a one-shot fetch (web useTrips has no live SSE subscription) — no
    >2-min staleness indicator is required for this unit (ADR-013 N/A here).
  - No #Preview blocks authored (this SDK's #Preview macro is ambiguous between
    SwiftUI and AppKit/UIKit, the documented baseline breakage) — keeps the unit
    clean-compiling; the Empty/Failing seams remain for the P9 XCTest phase.

